ssh3-c (0.4.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 0.4.0: the client -o options and the -R of
    the product client, the server --gateway-ports and
    --max-reverse-forwards, the event-loop UAF and idle-close fixes,
    the fd-0 close fixes of the channel free path, the honest failure
    counting of the test mains, and the audit closures (F-1/I-1/I-2
    closed, I-3 verified).
  * The Debian packaging wave joins the release: this source package
    (quilt 3.0, debhelper 13, lintian-clean CI in the trixie
    container) ships beside the bundled build.sh deb/rpm/apk whose
    private OpenSSL 3.5 copy keeps the older distributions covered.
  * The binary package is a drop-in replacement for ssh3-go:
    Provides/Conflicts/Replaces against the same /usr/bin interfaces.

 -- Max <nahual15@gmail.com>  Sun, 18 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0000

ssh3-c (0.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: ssh3-c 0.3.0, an independent C17 (nginx style)
    implementation of SSH3 - SSH over QUIC/HTTP3 (RFC 9220 extended
    CONNECT).
  * The product pair of 0.3.0: the ssh3-server daemon shipped here and
    the ssh3 client (built upstream, not part of this package).
  * The security-parity waves of the release cycle: per-session setuid
    of the root daemon, the sftp chroot jail, the DoS guard (unauth
    CONNECT cap, password lockout), forward policy knobs.
  * Client CLI aligned with the ssh(1) canon (-p, -l, -L, -R, -J, the
    config and agent surfaces).
  * Socket activation: the socket unit owns the UDP/443 QUIC listener
    (FreeBind, one datagram fd), the service unit stays static and
    comes up on the first packet.
  * Password login rides on against the unix accounts (the sshd
    PasswordAuthentication canon); the root account always fails the
    Basic step.  Bearer JWT and OIDC schemes complete the chain.

 -- Max <nahual15@gmail.com>  Sun, 18 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
